{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter at Work"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Presentation"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > Grammar - part 3 > The Suitcase"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 14}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le14ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Giving Presentations"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When delivering presentations, it is important to outline and organize what to say. We use:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">would like to</span> + <span class=\"italic\">verb</span> and the <span class=\"italic\">Present Simple</span> to introduce yourself and welcome the audience.  <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">\u201cHello everyone. I <span class=\"strong underline\">would like to start</span> by welcoming everyone. <span class=\"strong underline\">My name is</span> Jim Wilson and <span class=\"strong underline\">I'm an</span> HR expert.\u201d</span></li></ul></li> </ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">Present Simple</span>, <span class=\"italic\">will</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">going to</span>, to set the theme and introduce what you will be presenting. <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">\u201cThe purpose of this presentation <span class=\"strong underline\">is</span> to introduce our new learning software, which <span class=\"strong underline\">is going to be released</span> in two days.\u201d</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">\u201cToday I'<span class=\"strong underline\">m going to talk</span> about challenges and opportunities our company is facing.\u201d</span></li></ul></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">will</span> to give the audience a general outline of the presentation and <span class=\"italic\">sequence words</span> such as <span class=\"italic\">first</span>, <span class=\"italic\">then</span>, <span class=\"italic\">after that</span>, <span class=\"italic\">finally</span>.  <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">\u201c<span class=\"strong underline\">First</span>, I <span class=\"strong underline\">will</span> discuss some statistics and numbers. <span class=\"strong underline\">Then</span>, I <span class=\"strong underline\">will</span> outline some important points to be taken into consideration.\u201d</span></li></ul></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">What-clauses</span> can also be used to introduce topics and outline your presentation. <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">\u201c<span class=\"strong underline\">What we're going to look at</span> today is some statistics and numbers.\u201d</span></li></ul> </li></ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Stressing Content Words"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In English, we have two classes of words: <span class=\"strong\">content words</span> and <span class=\"strong\">function words</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">Function words</span> are words we use to make sentences grammatically correct.<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Pronouns</span>, <span class=\"italic\">determiners</span>, <span class=\"italic\">prepositions</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">conjunctions</span> are good examples.</li> <li><span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"strong\">Content words</span></span> are words that carry meaning.<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Nouns</span>, <span class=\"italic\">adjectives</span>, <span class=\"italic\">verbs</span> and <span class=\"italic\">adverbs</span> are all considered content words. </li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When speaking, we want the listener to have a better understanding of our story, so we make the <span class=\"strong\">content words</span> easier to hear by pronouncing them strongly. In other words, we add stress to them. <span class=\"strong\">Function words</span>, on the other hand, do not give the listener any relevant information. Therefore, they are not not stressed."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Hello <span class=\"strong\">everyone</span>. I'd <span class=\"strong\">like</span> to <span class=\"strong\">start</span> by <span class=\"strong\">welcoming</span> everyone. My <span class=\"strong\">name</span> is Marco de Angeli. I'm the <span class=\"strong\">head</span> of <span class=\"strong\">marketing</span> for <span class=\"strong\">All Foods</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Let</span> me <span class=\"strong\">begin</span> by <span class=\"strong\">presenting</span> a short <span class=\"strong\">outline</span> of my <span class=\"strong\">talk</span>. <span class=\"strong\">First</span>, I will <span class=\"strong\">discuss greetings</span> and <span class=\"strong\">opening conversation</span>."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "expectation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "beliefs about the way something should be"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I will discuss the expectations of time in my presentation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you may hear in a presentation at work."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "punctuality"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the quality of being on time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can discuss time and punctuality."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to initiate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to start"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In South America, the man usually waits for the woman to initiate a handshake."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "chatter"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "informal talk about things that are not serious or important"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some chatter is made in both cultures."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to break into"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to separate"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can break into small groups."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a topic you are interested in and want to learn more about."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Go on the internet and do some research on the topic. Make some notes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use your notes and create an outline for a presentation. Remember to include: an opening, an introduction to your topic, an overview of your presentation, at least 3 important points and a closing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you finish your outline, practice your presentation aloud."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Deliver your presentation to your class. Remember to stress content words and ask your class if they have any questions!"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I create an outline for a presentation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give a presentation on a topic of interest."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I stress content words when I speak."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "_