its for a woman to initiate a handshake. Meanwhile, this custom is no longer relevant in North America. Some small talk is made in both cultures, but a South American is usually more personable. For instance, it is normal for a North American to discuss the weather, but it is common for a South American to ask after a person's health or family. At this point, why don't we break into small groups and practice a few scenarios? I will hand out cards which identify you as a North or South American."}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": "Giving Presentations <br><br>1. Opening <br>\n2. Setting the theme <br>\n3. Giving an overview <br>\n4. Stating important points <br>\n5. Closing and questions"}], "video_src": "engenn6le14ob04re5vid01"}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "video", "id": 2, "_data": []}]}]}